WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.638
What if a historical question did not end in one answer, but unfolded through AI roles pushing the whole worldline forward?

00:00:09.638 --> 00:00:16.936
In SwarmOracle, you start with a question, set the parameters, and launch a real simulation.

00:00:16.936 --> 00:00:28.164
What appears next is not a single reply, but multiple roles taking different positions and pushing the same question in different directions.

00:00:28.164 --> 00:00:37.802
The whole exchange is mirrored into Pixel Theater, where characters, bubbles, scenes, and tension all shift in real time.

00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:40.461
You are not just watching, either.

00:00:40.461 --> 00:00:48.282
You can step in like a director, play cards, place bets, and push one worldline harder than another.

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:52.058
When the run ends, you do not just get an ending.

00:00:52.058 --> 00:00:57.452
You get a replayable, shareable record of how that outcome was formed.

00:00:57.452 --> 00:01:06.809
If you want a cleaner head-to-head clash, switch to Debate Arena and watch a five-phase argument move toward a verdict.

00:01:06.809 --> 00:01:13.920
SwarmOracle turns what-if questions into AI simulations you can watch, steer, and share.
